\item[Q.] 13 Which of the following statements about the instantaneous axis (passing through the centre of mass) is correct?
\begin{itemize}
\item[(A)] It is vertical for both the cases (a) and (b).
\item[(B)] It is vertical for case (a); and is at $45^{\circ}$ to the $x-z$ plane and lies in the plane of the disc for case (b).
\item[(C)] It is horizontal for case (a); and is at $45^{\circ}$ to the $x-z$ plane and is normal to the plane of the disc for case (b).
